{%- comment -%}
  schema-org — JewelryStore structured data for the business.

  Ported verbatim from the `custom-liquid` section on the old homepage, which
  is where it lived: a body section, at the bottom of the page, inside a
  container div. Structured data is head markup, not content — it has no
  visual output, so as a section it was invisible to the theme editor and could
  be dragged, disabled or deleted by accident. As a snippet it is emitted once,
  in <head>, on every page.

  RENDER IT FROM layout/theme.liquid, immediately before </head>:

      {% render 'schema-org' %}

  Two asset references carried over from the old block: fye-logo-square.png and
  fye-logo-wide.png. **Neither is in v3's assets/ yet** — binary files cannot be
  written into the repo from here, so they need uploading through Shopify admin
  (Content → Files is not enough; these must be theme assets). Until they are,
  the snippet falls back to the brand logo from Shopify's brand settings, and
  omits the keys entirely if that is empty too. An ld+json pointing at a 404 is
  worse than one with no image.

  The address is deliberately absent. JewelryStore inherits LocalBusiness,
  which wants a postal address, but FYE consults in person across London
  without a walk-in showroom — claiming a street address would be wrong, and
  Google penalises an address that cannot be verified. `areaServed` carries
  the geography instead. If a studio address is ever published, add
  `address` as a PostalAddress and Google will treat the listing as a
  storefront.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  assign logo_square = 'fye-logo-square.png' | asset_url
  assign logo_wide = 'fye-logo-wide.png' | asset_url
  if logo_square contains 'fye-logo-square.png'
    assign has_assets = true
  endif
  assign brand_logo = shop.brand.logo | image_url: width: 600
-%}
<script type="application/ld+json">
{
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "JewelryStore",
  "@id": "{{ shop.url }}/#business",
  "name": {{ shop.name | json }},
  "description": "Ethical engagement, wedding and eternity rings from a London jeweller. GIA/IGI-certified natural and lab-grown diamonds, transparent pricing, in-person and online consultations.",
  "url": "{{ shop.url }}",
  {%- if brand_logo != blank -%}
  "logo": "https:{{ brand_logo }}",
  "image": "https:{{ brand_logo }}",
  {%- elsif has_assets -%}
  "logo": "{{ logo_square | split: '//' | last | prepend: 'https://' }}",
  "image": "{{ logo_wide | split: '//' | last | prepend: 'https://' }}",
  {%- endif -%}
  "email": "hello@foryoureternity.com",
  "telephone": "+442081786687",
  "priceRange": "££",
  "currenciesAccepted": "GBP",
  "areaServed": [
    { "@type": "City", "name": "London" },
    { "@type": "Country", "name": "United Kingdom" }
  ],
  "sameAs": [
    "https://www.instagram.com/foryoureternityjewellery/"
  ],
  "potentialAction": {
    "@type": "ReserveAction",
    "target": "https://calendar.app.google/UKFkGvMLzAYEviqy8",
    "name": "Book a free consultation"
  }
}
</script>
